- Invalid provenance is rejected.
- Backend facts use typed provenance.
- Dynamic caller-facing text implying real-world dispatch is rejected and replaced by an approved phrase.

## 28.2a Provider-blocked content tests

- First blocked turn records an info `provider_blocked` audit event, plays the approved reassurance and re-ask prompt, and creates no flag and no assignment.
- The Nth consecutive blocked turn (default N = 2) with no established category triggers the fallback: category `unknown`, ambulance assignment, review flag with reason `provider_blocked_emergency_content`, fallback reason `consecutive_provider_blocks`.
- N is configurable, and the fallback fires at exactly N and never earlier.
- A schema-valid response between blocks resets `consecutive_provider_blocks`.
- Blocked turns never increment the unknown counter.
- A blocked turn with an established supported category creates no new assignment and sets only a warning flag at the Nth block.
- Further blocks after the fallback do not create additional assignments.
- Session end after one blocked turn with no established category triggers the fallback with reason `session_ended_after_provider_block`.
- Session end after blocks, where the fallback has already fired, creates no duplicate assignment.
- Reason codes `provider_blocked_emergency_content` and `reasoning_unavailable` are never interchanged.
- The required caller statement for the block fallback never claims real dispatch.
- No keyword classifier exists unless approved at Gate 0.13.
- A knife-attack scripted session (three consecutive blocked turns) ends with exactly one simulated ambulance assignment and a control-room flag.

